{"id":446,"slug":"pickup-on-south-street","title":"Pickup on South Street","year":1953,"country":"United States","duration":80,"spine":224,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/446-pickup-on-south-street","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/release_boxshots/4973-27ca119a58d66e036f2039b20b4d57d3/xwOFXh0wZIh9ZT2owG0fVQ0GcbIZ8Z_original.jpg","description":"Petty crook Skip McCoy (Richard Widmark) has his eyes fixed on the big score. When the cocky three-time convict picks the pocketbook of unsuspecting Candy (Jean Peters), he finds a more spectacular haul than he could have imagined: a strip of microfilm bearing confidential U.S. information. Tailed by manipulative Feds and the unwitting courier’s Communist puppeteers, Skip and Candy find themselves in a precarious gambit that pits greed against redemption, right against Red, and passion against self-preservation. With its dazzling cast and writer-director Samuel Fuller’s signature hard-boiled repartee and raw energy, Pickup on South Street is a true film noir classic by one of America’s most passionate cinematic craftspeople.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Samuel Fuller","slug":"samuel-fuller"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Richard Widmark","role":"Skip McCoy","slug":"richard-widmark"},{"actor":"Jean Peters","role":"Candy","slug":"jean-peters"},{"actor":"Thelma Ritter","role":"Moe","slug":"thelma-ritter"},{"actor":"Murvyn Vye","role":"Captain Dan Tiger","slug":"murvyn-vye"},{"actor":"Richard Kiley","role":"Joey","slug":"richard-kiley"},{"actor":"Willis B. Bouchey","role":"Zara","slug":"willis-b-bouchey"},{"actor":"Milburn Stone","role":"Winoki","slug":"milburn-stone"},{"actor":"Henry Slate","role":"MacGregor","slug":"henry-slate"},{"actor":"Victor Perry","role":"Lightning Louie","slug":"victor-perry"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Samuel Fuller","slug":"samuel-fuller"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Jules Schermer","slug":null},{"role":"Cinematography","person":"Joseph MacDonald","slug